Z||000050||JSocha||08-27-2001||10:21 AM||||Sorry to hear hoop.  I can imagine how tough a decision it was.  My father had to do the same thing with Boo Boo after a couple of surgery's to his neck after the tendon in his neck snapped.<P>We try and do everything for our pets, because of course, they become part of our lives.<P>When it comes to things like this, I believe we think we are all doing the best for them and making their lives fuller.  Instead, to our pets, I'm sure we are just prolonging the agony to which they have to endure just to satisfy our own beliefs that we are doing it for the better.<P>Its not easy.  Remember that at least Byng may not be suffering anymore and can rest much easier without pain or discomfort, knowing that you loved him enough to try what you could and that he loved you, if not the same, much more.<P>Again, sorry to hear.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000051||bHooper||08-27-2001||10:59 AM||||thanks, John, Raydar, and J!<P>it was very tough, our dog's are our children, but i did do the right thing.  <P>the other dog, Nick, is just starting to realize that Byng isn't coming back from the vet.  he's been mopeing all day.<P>hoop||||reg||1
